---
import Layout from "../layouts/home.astro";

// Rebuilt 2026-08-13 from Amy's "Amy Young - About-20260812.html" claude.ai/design export
// (unpacked with tools/unpack_bundler_export.py; source kept in Drive at
// "Web Development/Portfolio website_about/"). Replaces the 2026-08-07 build.
//
// What the new export adds over the 2026-08-07 page:
//  - A portrait + focus rail beside the hero, and "Based in Seattle, WA".
//  - A "My Story" section with a Read more expander (six paragraphs behind it).
//  - Systems became stat-led: each card now leads with a real number, not a faded "01".
//  - A six-item Toolkit accordion. Entirely new.
//  - Background merged Education and Recognition into ONE list beside a photo, instead
//    of two icon columns.
//
// Carried over unchanged, still confirmed:
//  - The CRG Research (1994-2011) / The Body Shop (1996-2009) overlap is correct and
//    intentional. She ran both concurrently. Do not "fix" the dates.
//  - "Public Information Specialist" is the real UW title (work/context/communications/
//    key-contacts.md), so the hero's "Information specialist by title ... and in practice"
//    does NOT contradict the "Communications & Funding Program Manager" role below it.
//  - Facts spot-checked against threads: Ubuntu 24.04 (ventures/context/infrastructure.md),
//    1,834 entities / 122 wiki pages (memory: project_openbrain).
//
// !! "I work at the intersection of data, product, and communications." — the hero's
// opening line. "At the intersection of" IS on the Never list in
// ventures/context/writing/style-guide.md -> "Site and Interface Copy" -> Worn
// constructions, and "at the crossroads of" was cut from this page on 2026-08-07 for
// being the same construction. It was flagged to Amy on 2026-08-13 and she RULED IT
// STAYS, with "communication" pluralized. Do not "fix" it again on a later pass.
//
// Two more were flagged and left as she wrote them: "Agentic" as a standing label (hero
// rail + Toolkit 01), and "cross-disciplinary thinking I've practiced my whole life".
//
// The only copy the port changed: em dashes in the Toolkit label/value pairs became
// colons (the style guide's em-dash rule is not NACC-only), and the Background section's
// sub-line ("Two degrees, one award from the NIA, and eleven years on a neighborhood
// board.") was cut on Amy's instruction 2026-08-13.

